<clickhouse>
  <!--
    The query-cost writer's principal (Phase 18b, Done-when 2). Identity lives in
    users.d like agent-ro.xml / metrics-ro.xml / allow-network.xml, reconstructed from
    this file at every container start — it cannot drift the way a SQL-created user in
    the mutable access/ store can.

    `cost_rw` is a WRITER, so it gets its OWN principal rather than widening the
    read-only metrics_ro (which stays SELECT-only on system metadata). Exactly two
    grants:
      - SELECT ON system.query_log — to read back the cost of the tagged report /
        restate / bench queries. Verified live (Phase 18b): a user with only this
        grant sees ANOTHER user's rows in system.query_log (query_log is not
        row-filtered per user the way system.parts is), so the default user runs the
        tagged queries and cost_rw reads their cost.
      - INSERT ON default.query_cost_daily — to write the per-query cost table, and
        nothing else. It cannot SELECT a single pipeline row: every read of
        attributed_conversions / exposures_landed / … is ACCESS_DENIED (code 497,
        verified live), the same posture as metrics_ro.

    Grant form, NOT <readonly>1</readonly> (it needs INSERT anyway): a SELECT/INSERT
    grant is enforced at the access-control layer and leaves the benign session
    settings clickhouse-connect sends on connect alone. Inline <grants> is supported
    since ClickHouse 22.4 (image is 24.8).

    `agent_ro`'s and `metrics_ro`'s grants are UNCHANGED — a third principal, not a
    wider existing one.

    Passwordless, ::/0, same local-dev posture as the other users.d principals: the
    host publishes 8123 on 127.0.0.1 only (compose), so the service stays off the LAN.
    Not for shared/multi-user hosts (BACKLOG). No secret is committed; a hardened
    deploy points CLICKHOUSE_COST_USER / _PASSWORD at its own credential, which lives
    in .env and never in CI.
  -->
  <users>
    <cost_rw>
      <password></password>
      <networks replace="replace">
        <ip>::/0</ip>
      </networks>
      <grants>
        <query>GRANT SELECT ON system.query_log</query>
        <query>GRANT INSERT ON default.query_cost_daily</query>
      </grants>
    </cost_rw>
  </users>
</clickhouse>
